# U87 TMZ/NanA synergy project

## What this project is
Combination cytotoxicity of temozolomide and nanaomycin A in U87MG
glioblastoma cells. MTT endpoint at 48 h and 72 h, four replicate plates
per time point, followed by an RT-PCR expression panel.

## Data layout
- `data/raw/` is read only. Never write to it, never edit a file in it,
  never offer to tidy one. If a raw file is wrong, we note it, we do not
  correct it.
- `data/clean/` holds outputs of `scripts/clean_*.py`. Everything here is
  regenerable and nothing here is edited by hand.
- `scripts/` holds the pipeline. Every cleaning script has a matching
  `gate_*.py` beside it.
- `figures/` is regenerated from scripts. Nothing is tuned by hand.

## Instrument exports
- SpectraCount MX-200 exports carry four preamble rows. The header is on
  row 6 and row 7 holds units, not data.
- A real well ID matches `[A-H]` followed by one or two digits. Anything
  else in the Well column is a footer row.
- The reader writes `OVER` when a well saturates and `<0.010` when a
  reading falls below threshold. Both are findings. Never coerce either
  to a blank.
- Some readings arrive as text rather than numbers. Parse explicitly.

## Units and naming
- Absorbance is at 595 nm. Column name `od595`, never `OD` or `abs`.
- Concentrations are micromolar. Column name `conc_uM`. If a file gives
  nanomolar, convert and say so in the output, do not mix.
- Time is in hours. Column name `time_h`, integer.
- Sample IDs appear as `U87_1`, `u87-1` and `U87 1`. Canonical form is
  `U87_<n>`. If an ID does not match that pattern, do not guess: flag it.
- Treatments are exactly: blank, DMSO, TMZ, NanA, TMZ+NanA.

## Rules for any analysis in this project
- Never use `errors='coerce'`. Parse explicitly and record what failed.
- Never drop a row silently. A row is either carried through or written
  to an exclusions file with a reason column.
- Do not aggregate unless the task asks for it. Cleaning means one row
  per well, not a mean.
- Blank wells are excluded from treatment statistics, never averaged in.
- Report effect sizes with confidence intervals, not p-values alone.

## Before you tell me a task is done
- The matching `gate_*.py` must run and pass.
- Print counts: rows in, rows kept, rows excluded. They must reconcile.
- If you changed a script, say which gate you ran and what it printed.

## Things that have gone wrong before
- A units row read as data, which shifted every dtype in the frame.
- A silent `coerce` that dropped two saturated wells and changed a mean.
- A time column parsed as text, so a gate compared strings and passed
  for the wrong reason.
